>> title: Potato Leek Soup
>> servings: 8
>> source: my mom

> Potato leek soup is a forgiving recipe and it will forgive you for any culinary mistakes you may make. 

Halve a @leek{1}(large) and rinse each half to remove any silt between the layers. Chop each half into thin slices, discarding the leafy dark green portion of the leek. 

In a #stock pot{}, heat @butter{4%tbsp} of medium heat until it becomes frothy. Add the leek to the pot and stir to combine with the butter. Reduce heat to low, cover the pot, and let cook for ~{7%minutes}. 

While the leek cooks, wash and peel @russet potatoes{4-5}. Chop into 1-inch sized cubes.

Once the leek has finished cooking, add the potatoes to the stock pot along with @vegetable stock{4%cups}. Increase heat to medium, cover the pot, and let cook for ~{25%minutes} or until potatoes have softened. 

Remove pot from the heat and mash potatoes until a soup-like consistency is achieved. You can use a #potato masher or blender{} for this, depending on your desired consistency. 

Season with @salt{}(to taste) and @pepper{}(to taste). Sprinkle with @parsely{} as garnish and enjoy while hot. 

> This soup is best enjoyed when accompanied with fresh bread.